---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '29 July 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy & GDPR Policy — The Boat Yard Sauna"
  description="How The Boat Yard Sauna collects, uses, stores, and protects your personal information."
>
  <article class="policy section">
    <div class="container policy__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy &amp; GDPR</p>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="policy__updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <div class="policy__lead">
        <p>
          This notice explains how The Boat Yard Sauna handles your personal data when you use this
          website, join our mailing list, buy a gift voucher, contact us, or follow a link to book a
          sauna session.
        </p>
      </div>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Who controls your data</h2>
        <p>
          The data controller is The Boat Yard Sauna, operating at Wicklow Harbour, Wicklow Town,
          and North Quay, Arklow Harbour, Ireland.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy enquiries and data-rights requests can be sent to
          <a href="mailto:theboatyardsauna@gmail.com">theboatyardsauna@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Your email address when you subscribe to updates.</li>
          <li>
            Voucher purchase details, including the buyer’s name and email, payment confirmation,
            and any recipient name, recipient email, or gift message you provide.
          </li>
          <li>Information you include when contacting us directly.</li>
          <li>
            Technical security information normally created when a website is accessed, such as an
            IP address, browser type, request time, and server logs.
          </li>
          <li>
            Booking information collected on an external booking service when you follow a booking
            link. That service will also provide its own privacy notice.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Please only provide another person’s details for a voucher if you have their permission
          to do so.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Why we use it and our legal basis</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            To process purchases, issue vouchers, answer booking enquiries, and provide requested
            services. Our basis is performance of a contract or steps requested before a contract.
          </li>
          <li>
            To send mailing-list updates. Our basis is your consent, which you can withdraw at any
            time by using the unsubscribe link or contacting us.
          </li>
          <li>
            To keep financial and transaction records where required by law. Our basis is
            compliance with a legal obligation.
          </li>
          <li>
            To protect the website, prevent fraud, resolve problems, and respond to claims. Our
            basis is our legitimate interests in operating a secure and accountable service.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell your personal data.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Services that receive data</h2>
        <p>We share only the information needed with service providers that help us operate:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Stripe, for secure voucher payments.</li>
          <li>Resend, for delivery of voucher emails.</li>
          <li>Buttondown, for mailing-list subscriptions and emails.</li>
          <li>Our external booking provider, when you choose to make a booking.</li>
          <li>Vercel, which hosts this website and may process technical request logs.</li>
          <li>Sanity, which provides the website’s content-management service.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may also disclose information where the law requires it or where necessary to protect
          legal rights. Some providers may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where
          that happens, the provider must use a lawful transfer mechanism and appropriate
          safeguards, such as an adequacy decision or standard contractual clauses.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Mailing-list details are kept until you unsubscribe or withdraw consent.</li>
          <li>
            Transaction and accounting records are kept for the period required by Irish law,
            generally six years.
          </li>
          <li>
            Voucher delivery details and correspondence are kept only as long as needed to provide
            the voucher, handle queries, and establish or defend legal claims.
          </li>
          <li>
            Security logs are retained for a limited period appropriate to website security and
            troubleshooting.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>We securely delete or anonymise personal data when it is no longer needed.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
        <p>
          This website does not currently use advertising or analytics cookies. It uses essential
          browser storage only to remember your cookie preference. This does not track you between
          websites and is not used for advertising. Optional analytics cookies are currently
          switched off and will not load unless we add them in the future and you actively choose
          to accept them.
        </p>
        <p>
          External services opened from this website, including booking and payment services, may
          use their own necessary or optional cookies under their own policies and consent
          controls. If we add analytics, advertising, or other optional tracking to this website,
          it will remain disabled until you make an informed choice.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Your GDPR rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on the circumstances, you may ask us for access to your personal data, to
          correct it, erase it, restrict its use, object to its use, or provide it in a portable
          format. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw that consent at any time
          without affecting earlier lawful processing.
        </p>
        <p>
          Email your request to
          <a href="mailto:theboatyardsauna@gmail.com">theboatyardsauna@gmail.com</a>. We may need to
          verify your identity before acting. You also have the right to complain to Ireland’s
          <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Data Protection Commission
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Security, children, and changes</h2>
        <p>
          We use appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data, but no
          internet service can guarantee absolute security. This website and its purchasing tools
          are not directed at children acting independently. A parent or guardian should make any
          booking or purchase involving a child.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may update this notice when our services or legal obligations change. The date at the
          top shows the latest revision.
        </p>
      </section>

      <div class="policy__accept">
        <button class="btn btn--primary" id="policy-accept" type="button">Accept &amp; continue</button>
        <p id="policy-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<script>
  const button = document.getElementById('policy-accept');
  const status = document.getElementById('policy-status');
  button?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    try {
      localStorage.setItem('boatyard-privacy-notice-v1', 'accepted');
    } catch {
      // Continue even when browser storage is blocked.
    }
    if (status) status.textContent = 'Your acknowledgement has been saved on this device.';
    button.textContent = 'Accepted';
    (button as HTMLButtonElement).disabled = true;
  });
</script>

<style>
  .policy {
    padding-top: clamp(7rem, 14vw, 10rem);
  }

  .policy__inner {
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  .policy h1 {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
  }

  .policy__updated {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }

  .policy__lead {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 3.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--cedar);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.2rem, 2.5vw, 1.55rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .policy section + section {
    margin-top: 2.75rem;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.5vw, 1.9rem);
    font-weight: 480;
  }

  .policy p,
  .policy li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .policy p + p,
  .policy ul + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .policy ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .policy a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
  }

  .policy__accept {
    margin-top: 3.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--mist-10);
  }

  .policy__accept p {
    min-height: 1.5em;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    font-size: var(--text-small);
  }
</style>
